---
import UntranslatedLayout from '~/layouts/UntranslatedLayout.astro';
import { ArrowLeft, ShieldCheck, Database, Megaphone, Activity, ExternalLink } from 'lucide-react';
---

<UntranslatedLayout
  title="Beat Expert Privacy Policy | BeHonor Studio"
  description="Beat Expert privacy policy: local music projects and recordings, Beat Points, Google AdMob and UMP, Firebase Analytics and Crashlytics, backups and deletion."
>
  <article class="pt-32 pb-24">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6">
      <header class="mb-10">
        <a href="/products/drumpads/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-medium text-primary hover:text-primary/80 transition-colors group mb-6">
          <ArrowLeft className="w-4 h-4 group-hover:-translate-x-1 transition-transform" />
          Back to Beat Expert
        </a>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-6">
          <img
            src="/images/apps/beat_expert_icon.png"
            alt="Beat Expert app icon"
            width="64"
            height="64"
            class="w-16 h-16 object-contain rounded-2xl shadow-md shrink-0"
          />
          <div>
            <span class="block text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-primary">BeHonor Studio · Android</span>
            <span class="block text-xs text-muted-foreground mt-1">Beat Expert: Drum Pads</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold mb-4 font-display text-foreground">
          Privacy Policy for Beat Expert
        </h1>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">Effective date: November 5, 2026 · Last updated: November 6, 2026</p>
        <a
          href="https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.behonor.drumpads"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 mt-6 text-sm text-primary font-medium"
        >
          Google Play <ExternalLink className="w-3.5 h-3.5" />
        </a>
      </header>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 mb-12">
        <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-emerald-500/10 border border-emerald-500/20">
          <Database className="w-7 h-7 text-emerald-500 mb-3" />
          <h2 class="font-semibold text-foreground text-sm">Beats stay on your device</h2>
          <p class="text-xs text-muted-foreground mt-2">Your projects, pad recordings, imported-audio references and Beat Points are stored locally.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-indigo-500/10 border border-indigo-500/20">
          <Megaphone className="w-7 h-7 text-indigo-500 mb-3" />
          <h2 class="font-semibold text-foreground text-sm">Rewarded ads are optional</h2>
          <p class="text-xs text-muted-foreground mt-2">AdMob and UMP support opt-in rewarded ads and applicable privacy choices.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-amber-500/10 border border-amber-500/20">
          <Activity className="w-7 h-7 text-amber-500 mb-3" />
          <h2 class="font-semibold text-foreground text-sm">Third-party data is disclosed</h2>
          <p class="text-xs text-muted-foreground mt-2">Firebase Analytics and Crashlytics process usage events and technical crash reports.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <section id="english" lang="en" class="policy-section scroll-mt-32">
        <div class="prose dark:prose-invert max-w-none text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed prose-headings:font-display prose-headings:text-foreground prose-a:text-primary">
          <p class="text-lg font-medium text-foreground">
            BeHonor Studio (“we”, “our”, “us”) provides Beat Expert: Drum Pads, an Android rhythm-creation app
            (package name: <code>com.behonor.drumpads</code>). This policy applies to Beat Expert only.
            It describes how local music data, advertising, analytics and crash diagnostics are handled.
            For questions or privacy requests, contact <a href="mailto:beehonorstu@gmail.com">beehonorstu@gmail.com</a>.
          </p>
          <p>Beat Expert does not require an account. Its drum pads, beat editor and imported backing music primarily work locally, but the released app also uses network-based Google services. We therefore do not claim that the app is entirely offline or that no technical data is collected.</p>

          <h3>1. Music projects, recordings and local storage</h3>
          <p>Beat Expert lets you play drum pads, compose rhythms, import backing audio, record pad performances, save and share editable projects, and export WAV or MP3 audio. Your works, recorded pad events, app settings and references to imported audio are stored on your Android device. Pad-performance recording captures taps and musical timing inside the app; it does <strong>not</strong> use the microphone or request microphone permission.</p>
          <p>The app does not operate an account system or a developer-hosted server for uploading your songs, recorded performances or selected audio files. When you choose to export or share, Android transfers the file or content to the destination you select; that destination's privacy practices also apply. Your original imported files remain at their original location unless you remove them separately.</p>

          <h3>2. Beat Points and unlock information</h3>
          <p>Beat Expert offers a local points balance: a daily check-in earns 10 points, an optional rewarded ad may earn 25 points after the provider confirms the reward, and 100 points unlocks one official beat permanently in this installation. The first two official beats are available without points. Points have no monetary value, cannot be transferred and are not linked to an account.</p>
          <p>The app stores its points balance, check-in state and unlocked-beat identifiers in a protected local ledger backed by Android Keystore. The ledger is specifically excluded from Android backup and device-transfer rules because its encryption keys cannot be safely restored on another installation. Your points or purchased-with-points beat access may therefore be lost when the app is uninstalled, its data is cleared, or you move to a new device. This system is separate from the temporary drum-kit reward described below.</p>

          <h3>3. AdMob rewarded ads and Google UMP consent</h3>
          <p>Beat Expert uses <strong>Google AdMob / Google Mobile Ads (GMA Next-Gen)</strong> for optional rewarded video advertisements, along with Google's <strong>User Messaging Platform (UMP)</strong> for consent and privacy choices where applicable. The app checks UMP consent availability before initiating advertising requests. Once allowed, the advertising SDK may initialize and preload an ad before you choose to watch one. Playback of a rewarded advertisement begins only when you explicitly request it.</p>
          <p>Google's advertising systems may automatically collect or share information including IP address and approximate location inferred from it, device or advertising identifiers (such as Android advertising ID where available), app and ad interactions, impression and click data, device and app properties, and performance or diagnostic information. Google and its partners may use these signals for delivering and measuring advertising, preventing abuse and fraud, or other purposes described in Google's policies. Non-personalized or limited advertising may still involve processing necessary for security, delivery or measurement.</p>
          <p>Jazz is always free. When you choose to watch a rewarded ad and the SDK confirms a reward, the other four drum kits unlock together for <strong>24 hours</strong>; the expiration time is kept locally. If an ad is unavailable, cancelled or not rewarded, no unlock is granted. Watching ads is optional for the basic app, although rewards themselves require the advertising service and network access.</p>
          <p>Where UMP requires it, an “Ad privacy choices” entry in Settings lets you review or adjust the options presented, including withdrawal or opt-out where available. You can also manage or delete your Android advertising ID through supported Android settings. Consent to ad personalization is separate from your choice to watch a rewarded ad.</p>
          <p>See <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Privacy Policy</a>, <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's information use in partner apps</a> and <a href="https://developers.google.com/admob/android/next-gen/privacy/play-data-disclosure" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Mobile Ads data disclosure</a>.</p>

          <h3>4. Firebase Analytics and Crashlytics</h3>
          <p>The released app includes <strong>Google Analytics for Firebase</strong> and <strong>Firebase Crashlytics</strong>. Analytics helps us understand app usage; Crashlytics helps us detect and fix faults. Beat Expert logs named screen visits and limited feature-use events, such as playback, saving a beat, starting a recording, and rewarded-ad events. Some custom events include bounded numeric settings such as BPM or number of bars. We do not intentionally attach project contents, imported audio, song titles or recorded pad-event sequences to custom analytics events.</p>
          <p>Firebase may automatically process app-instance or installation identifiers, app/OS version, device information, event timing and crash diagnostics. Crashlytics may receive stack traces and technical app state; the app also supplies fixed diagnostic labels such as app brand, build type and current screen. Diagnostic reports should not be assumed to be fully anonymous. Firebase processing is distinct from AdMob processing, even though both are Google services.</p>
          <p>Firebase Analytics and Crashlytics are enabled in the released app. Beat Expert does not currently offer a separate in-app switch to disable all Firebase collection, and UMP's advertising choices are not a global switch for Firebase telemetry. Learn more: <a href="https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Firebase Privacy and Security</a>.</p>

          <h3>5. Android permissions and sharing</h3>
          <p>The app uses internet and network-state access for advertising, consent and Firebase services. Basic drum performance and editing do not require microphone, camera, contacts or precise location permissions. Importing backing audio uses Android's document picker, and exporting or sharing uses the file picker or Android sharing mechanisms. The app does not automatically upload your audio projects to BeHonor Studio.</p>

          <h3>6. Retention, backups and deletion</h3>
          <p>You can delete saved works with the app's available controls and remove imported-audio references. Clearing Beat Expert's Android app data or uninstalling it normally removes its private local records from that device. Copy or export any music you wish to keep first. Removing the app does not remove original audio files outside the app, files you exported, items you shared, or data already held by another service.</p>
          <p>Android system backup and device transfer are allowed for some app data, depending on your Android settings and backup provider. <strong>The protected Beat Points ledger is excluded from backup and transfer</strong>; other local projects and preferences may be included in backup or transferred and restored. You can review Android backup settings on your device. Third-party advertising, analytics and diagnostic records are handled under their providers' retention practices; clearing the app does not instantly delete those records.</p>

          <h3>7. Support messages and privacy requests</h3>
          <p>If you contact us, we receive the email address and information you choose to include, which we use to respond to your question or resolve support requests. Depending on your jurisdiction, you may have rights to access, correct, delete, restrict or object to processing, withdraw consent, opt out or lodge a complaint. Contact us about information we control; Google provides separate controls and request channels for information it processes.</p>

          <h3>8. Security and international processing</h3>
          <p>Local information is handled using Android's storage mechanisms and available device protections. Third-party services may process technical and advertising data in countries other than yours, using their own security measures and policies. No storage or transfer method can guarantee absolute security.</p>

          <h3>9. Children's privacy</h3>
          <p>Beat Expert is not designed specifically for children under 13. We do not knowingly collect children's personal information through a developer-operated account or music-upload service. If you believe a child has provided information through a support request, contact us. Advertising and Firebase services follow the data practices described above.</p>

          <h3>10. Changes and contact</h3>
          <p>We may update this policy when our features, service providers or legal requirements change. The date above identifies the latest revision. Privacy and support: <a href="mailto:beehonorstu@gmail.com">beehonorstu@gmail.com</a>.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <div class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-foreground/10 flex gap-3 items-center text-sm text-muted-foreground">
        <ShieldCheck className="w-5 h-5 text-emerald-500 shrink-0" />
        <span>This policy applies to the Beat Expert: Drum Pads Android app, not to other BeHonor Studio products.</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</UntranslatedLayout>
